## How to Apply the PaperStream License to Your Own Program

To apply this License to a new program, attach the following notice to the beginning of each source file:

```
[Program Name] — [Short description, e.g. "A Paper plugin for ..."]
Copyright (C) [Year] [Author Name]
A [ORGANIZATION] project.

This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
it under the terms of the PaperStream License (PSL) v1.0.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but
WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
See the PaperStream License for more details.

A copy of the license should have been distributed with this program
(see LICENSE.md). If not, see [LINK TO YOUR REPO]/LICENSE.md.
```

Also place this file as `LICENSE.md` in the root directory of each project. Fill in **[YEAR]**, **[AUTHOR NAME]**, **[PROJECT NAME]**, **[ORGANIZATION]**, and the **Description** at the top of the file individually for each project — this keeps a single license template reusable across all repositories.
